This assumes that you have a wand of polymorph available. Even if you
do, imagine the situation where like: you're in Vlads, you have +4
gloves of dex and +4 helm of brilliance. Your AK is just about
complete. Get a throne wish. Man, I really wish I had drain life so I
could get magic mapping to 0% failure. Should I get the marker or the
book? Of course you could argue and I wouldn't necessarily disagree
that there are better things to do with a wish at that point. Maybe a
wand of death. Hell, maybe a wand of polymorph. I'm not trying to say
that my above math is the be-all and end-all to the discussion;
hardly, if it was, Nethack wouldn't be as fun as it is. But I found
myself in a situation where I wanted drain life and had a spare wish
and wasn't sure what was best, so I did the math. And then I got both
drain life and both enchant armor scrolls out of my fresh marker and a
charging scroll and charges to spare. P.S. I was in the castle with a
1:3 wand and a complete AK in my actual situation.

